&lt;p&gt;Did you know that the .NET compiler turns our async methods into a struct? And that .NET adds a try/catch block to each of these classes, potentially hiding thrown exceptions? It&amp;rsquo;s true!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this session, we will learn how to best use async/await in C# by analyzing how .NET compiles our async code.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>